    {
      "name" : "non-pair-tuple-spend-eq_any_operands#4",
      "source" : "santa:authored-non-pair-tuple-spend",
      "description" : "`sigmaProp(t(0) == t(1))` — **THE CROSS-TIER KEYSTONE.** The wire family's `eq-any-any-v3` has this exact tree ACCEPTED and round-tripping byte-identically (the deserialization builder's SameType check is satisfied when both operands are `SAny`), and here the spend is **INVALID**, because `Value.checkType`/`isValueOfType` has no `SAny` case at all. A box anyone can create and nobody can spend. **SEPARATING THE OTHER WAY.**",
